# [CompliRules] EU AI Act (Reg. 2024/1689) Article 5 Prohibited AI Practices Invariants
**Severity:** `CRITICAL` | **Jurisdiction:** `AI_ACT_EU`

<!-- NOTICE: CompliRules provides automated AST guardrails under CompliRules Free-to-Use License without warranty (See DISCLAIMER.md). Documentation: https://halilyilmz.github.io/complirules/ -->

## Legal Citations
- **Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 (EU Artificial Intelligence Act) (Article 5(1)(f))**: Prohibition of AI systems to infer emotions of a natural person in the areas of workplace and education institutions. *[Sanction: Article 99(3) administrative fines up to €35,000,000 or 7% of total worldwide annual turnover. Effective date: 2 February 2025.]*
- **Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 (EU Artificial Intelligence Act) (Article 5(1)(e))**: Prohibition of creating or expanding facial recognition databases through the untargeted scraping of facial images from the internet or CCTV footage.
- **Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 (EU Artificial Intelligence Act) (Article 5(1)(c))**: Prohibition of AI-driven social scoring evaluating trustworthiness based on social conduct or personality traits.

## Rule Mandates
- MUST: NEVER implement emotion recognition models (e.g. DeepFace.analyze(actions=["emotion"]), AWS Rekognition Emotions, Affectiva) in workplace, recruitment, or educational software (Art. 5(1)(f)).
- MUST: NEVER build scrapers harvesting profile pictures or facial images from public web pages into facial recognition vector databases (Art. 5(1)(e)).
- MUST: NEVER implement social trustworthiness scoring algorithms evaluating individuals based on social conduct (Art. 5(1)(c)).
- MUST: MUST raise ProhibitedPracticeViolation on attempts to deploy prohibited capabilities in sensitive contexts.

## Forbidden Anti-Patterns
- NEVER: Emotion recognition classification in HR/recruitment or education proctoring
- NEVER: Untargeted web scraping of facial images for biometric recognition databases
- NEVER: Social scoring algorithms evaluating individual conduct

